messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Global energy-related CO2 emissions peak.",
      "detail": "Solar, wind, and battery deployment outpace growth in coal and oil demand. Emissions plateau and begin a slow decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Humanoid robots begin large-scale warehouse deployment.",
      "detail": "They handle sorting, packing, and loading under human supervision, reducing costs in e-commerce."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "A severe wet-bulb heatwave kills tens of thousands in South Asia and the Persian Gulf.",
      "detail": "Humidity and temperature exceed safe human limits for several hours. It accelerates adaptation investment and migration."
    },
    {
      "year": 2036,
      "event": "An AI-assisted cyberattack causes a cascading grid failure in a major economy.",
      "detail": "The blackout lasts several days and reveals vulnerabilities in energy control systems. It leads to stricter AI and infrastructure security rules."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "First broad-spectrum AI-designed antibiotics enter clinical use.",
      "detail": "Machine learning models screen large chemical spaces against resistant bacteria. New drugs restore effectiveness against several resistant infections."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "World population reaches about 9.2 billion.",
      "detail": "Fertility is below replacement in most countries, but growth continues because of age structure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2044,
      "event": "First AGI-like systems pass broad tests of reasoning and planning.",
      "detail": "They still require large compute and human oversight, but they outperform most humans on many cognitive tasks. This triggers major governance efforts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "A crewed Mars landing establishes a temporary base.",
      "detail": "Crew stays for one surface mission and returns. The base is later expanded with robotic supply flights."
    },
    {
      "year": 2052,
      "event": "Major coastal cities complete first-generation sea defenses.",
      "detail": "Repeated flooding forces large investments in barriers, pumps, and raised districts. Some low-lying areas are abandoned."
    },
    {
      "year": 2056,
      "event": "A global climate migration framework is adopted.",
      "detail": "Tens of millions of people have moved because of heat, water stress, and sea-level rise. The framework sets rules for resettlement and funding."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Global population begins to decline.",
      "detail": "Deaths exceed births worldwide as fertility falls, including in most of Africa."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Commercial fusion plants begin supplying electricity in several countries.",
      "detail": "Fusion is technically successful but initially expensive. It complements renewables and helps power carbon removal."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Large-scale carbon dioxide removal reaches about 2 billion tonnes per year.",
      "detail": "Direct air capture, enhanced weathering, and reforestation are operating at scale. The world becomes net-negative in emissions by this decade."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Sea level rise reaches about 0.5 m above 2000 levels.",
      "detail": "Managed retreat is underway in vulnerable deltas and island states. Some nations continue through resettlement agreements."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Global mean temperature stabilizes near +2.1°C above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Damages are severe but adaptation and negative emissions prevent worst-case runaway warming."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Earth's population stabilizes near 6 billion with a much older age structure.",
      "detail": "Many countries have shrunk, while a few rebound through pro-natal and migration policies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "A permanent lunar settlement grows to several thousand people.",
      "detail": "Water ice mining and research support the early economy. Tourism and science expand it."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Mars settlement reaches about 50,000 people and becomes self-sufficient in food.",
      "detail": "Hardened greenhouses and 3D-printed habitats support life. The colony still depends on Earth for advanced equipment."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Genetic screening and embryo selection eliminate most single-gene diseases.",
      "detail": "Polygenic screening raises ethical debates and access remains unequal. New gene therapies cure many inherited conditions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Automation and abundant energy make basic goods very cheap in most regions.",
      "detail": "Labor shifts toward care, creativity, governance, and leisure. Poverty is rare but not abolished."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Nation-states weaken as primary governing units.",
      "detail": "City networks and planetary institutions manage climate, migration, and shared resources. National identity persists but sovereignty is shared."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Industrial animal farming is largely replaced by cultured meat and engineered crops.",
      "detail": "Synthetic biology produces most protein and fats. Large areas of pasture are rewilded."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "A planetary asteroid and comet deflection system becomes operational.",
      "detail": "A test successfully shifts a small asteroid. The system later prevents at least one major impact."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Sea level stabilizes after rising 1-2 m since 2000.",
      "detail": "Ice sheets reach a new equilibrium. Coastal cities are rebuilt inland or raised."
    },
    {
      "year": 2900,
      "event": "Median human lifespan reaches 110-120 years in wealthy communities.",
      "detail": "Senescence therapies slow multiple aging processes. Aging is not ended, and unequal access remains."
    },
    {
      "year": 3100,
      "event": "Earth's biosphere shows large-scale recovery.",
      "detail": "Carbon removal and reduced land use allow forests and wetlands to expand. Biodiversity begins to increase after centuries of decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Mars population exceeds one million and becomes semi-autonomous.",
      "detail": "Trade with Earth is limited by launch costs. Cultural and political divergence grows."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Rotating space habitats house hundreds of thousands in Earth orbit.",
      "detail": "They specialize in zero-gravity industry, energy collection, and medicine. Some become independent city-states."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "The first interstellar robotic probe reaches Proxima Centauri.",
      "detail": "It confirms a rocky planet but no sign of life. The signal takes 4.2 years to return to Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Human-origin intelligences spread throughout the inner solar system.",
      "detail": "Most are biological humans; others are augmented or digital offshoots. Earth remains the largest population center."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Earth's climate stabilizes near a new warm state without large-scale geoengineering.",
      "detail": "Atmospheric CO2 falls toward 350 ppm. Large-scale removal is no longer needed."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Human descendants on Earth, Mars, and habitats are culturally and genetically distinct.",
      "detail": "They remain mutually intelligible with translation. No full speciation occurs."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Space-based solar collection begins transitioning toward Dyson-scale use.",
      "detail": "Most energy used by civilization comes from space. Earth is increasingly reserved for ecology and heritage."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Robotic seed ships carrying human genetic material depart to nearby systems.",
      "detail": "These are multi-century projects with uncertain outcomes. They aim to establish colonies around other stars."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity exists as a multi-planet, multi-habitat civilization.",
      "detail": "Population across the solar system is in the billions; biology and machine intelligence are deeply intertwined. Earth remains the symbolic center."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "The 21st century is likely to be a period of climate disruption, demographic transition, and AI transformation. I do not expect extinction by 10000; instead, civilization becomes multi-planetary and biologically and culturally diverse, while recovering from environmental damage."
}
